BEGIN BODY-W1
BLUF: At main <<MAIN8>>, startingOwner (web/src/components/customer/remediation-store.ts) keeps a lone high surrogate that is the 100th unit: for 99 letters, one lone high surrogate (U+D83D) and then the letter b, the result is 100 units ending in the lone surrogate, and b is not added. The code before pull request 327 returned the same, so no behaviour changed; no test row pins it, and HPSMPOC-505 (Done by pull request 329) named the case and left it out. The register is kept in the browser tab only (the file's own header comment, line 2), so the effect is small; this ticket exists so the case is decided once and not found again.
Recommendation: Decide what the result should be, then pin it with one row in the startingOwner block: keep it as it is (100 units; the register's own check refuses an owner only by length, remediation-store.ts:45, so it accepts that result), or end the result before a lone high surrogate that would be its last unit. Tests first: the row's expected value is the decision. Proposed default if nobody chooses: pin the current result with one row (tests only; no product line changes).
Detail: From the independent review of pull request 327 (its finding 5, a Minor): "A lone-surrogate input stays lone in the result when the lone surrogate is the 100th unit". The same Minor is named in HPSMPOC-505's Detail. In the function (remediation-store.ts:58 to :72 at main <<MAIN8>>) the loop walks the grapheme segments of the trimmed owner and stops at the first one that would pass the limit (the comparison is at :68); a lone surrogate is a one-unit segment, so it is added when it is the 100th unit (DERIVED from the loop; the person who drafted this ticket also ran a copy of those lines once in Node 26: 100 units, last unit U+D83D, b not added; not run on the project's pinned Node version). Not measured: what a real owner value could put in that position; the result on the pinned Node version. Nothing is changed by this ticket.
Done when: a row that pins the result for 99 letters, a lone high surrogate and then b (whichever result is decided) is in the suite and passes, or the item is recorded as declined.
Records: entry C-<<CE3>> in the project's clarifications record.
