### W2: the Next.js advisory GHSA-mfr8-8qww-v76h (create; Task; priority Medium; labels `rec-2026-11-17`, `follow-up`, `dependabot`; marker `REC-LND5-17NOV-W2`)
SUMMARY-W2: next 16.4.2 (web/package.json:20) is inside the range of GHSA-mfr8-8qww-v76h (medium; vulnerable 16.3.0 to 16.4.4, first patched 16.4.5); the web app uses neither 'use cache' nor unstable_cache, so it reads as not reached; upgrade as a normal change

BEGIN BODY-W2
BLUF: The web app pins next at 16.4.2 (web/package.json:20 and the lock, at main <<MAIN8>>). GitHub published GHSA-mfr8-8qww-v76h (CVE-2026-119790, medium, CWE-362) on 2026-11-16: with 'use cache', cached data can cross root params when the same function is called both directly and through unstable_cache() during a cold start; the vulnerable range is 16.3.0 to 16.4.4 and the first patched release is 16.4.5. Two Dependabot alerts are open for it (alerts 10 and 11: package.json and the lock; runtime, direct; created 2026-11-17). The app appears not to use the feature: a search of the repository finds neither unstable_cache nor 'use cache', and web/next.config.ts holds no cache setting. So this reads as an advisory against a pin the app is in range of, not as an exposure; that reading is DERIVED, not measured by running anything.
Recommendation: Upgrade next to a patched release (16.4.5 or later in the 16.4 line) in its own small change: web/package.json and the lock only, no code, then the whole web suite, a build and the end-to-end checks, and ship it with the next update the product owner approves. Proposed default if nobody chooses: that change. This ticket accepts nothing and approves no upgrade.
Detail: Read at main <<MAIN8>>. The advisory record (GitHub): published 2026-11-16T18:51:22Z, severity medium, vulnerable range ">= 16.3.0, <= 16.4.4", first patched release 16.4.5. The CI audit steps use a high bar (npm audit --omit=dev --audit-level=high), so this medium finding does not turn CI red; the builders' runs print "1 moderate severity vulnerability" for it. Locally, the first npm run build in each tree stops once with a Next.js security notice and passes when the same command is repeated; both builders and the independent review saw it, and none of them ran an upgrade or touched a package file. One builder's note named 16.4.6 as the fix; the advisory record and both alerts read 16.4.5. Not measured: whether a build at 16.4.5 changes any behaviour the web tests pin. Searched at filing: no ticket names this advisory or the upgrade (the phrase searches for the advisory id, for unstable_cache and for next upgrade read 0); HPSMPOC-478 and HPSMPOC-346 are dependency tickets about other packages.
Done when: next is at a patched release (16.4.5 or later) in web/package.json and the lock, the web suite and a build are green and both Dependabot alerts are closed, or the item is recorded as declined with its reason.
Records: entry C-<<CE3>> in the project's clarifications record.
Marker: [REC-LND5-17NOV-W2]
END BODY-W2

